Upstream defect: `wren context import dbt` crashes on model-level dbt tests
===========================================================================

Found while integrating WrenAI 0.13.2 into code-skills, against
skill-packs/dbt-skills/use-cases/example-order-revenue-mart (a dbt project with
singular and model-level dbt_utils tests, both of which carry `column_name: None`
in manifest.json).

`_build_verified_constraint_lines` groups test events by `(model_name, column_name)`
and sorts the dict items. A None column name makes `sorted()` compare None to str:

    TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'str'

The importer already skips columnless entries *inside* the loop (`if not
column_name: continue`) — the crash is only in the sort key, one line earlier.

Local workaround: scripts/wren_context_sync.py filters model-level test rows out
of run_results.json for the duration of the import (see
`_model_level_tests_hidden`). Remove that workaround when this fix ships in the
pinned wrenai wheel, and bump the pin in requirements.txt together with the
external/WrenAI submodule SHA.

To apply to the fork (PackMaaan/WrenAI) and send upstream:

    cd external/WrenAI
    git apply ../patches/wrenai-dbt-import-columnless-tests.patch
    # commit on a branch, push to the fork, open a PR against Canner/WrenAI

--- a/core/wren/src/wren/dbt.py
+++ b/core/wren/src/wren/dbt.py
@@ -1198,7 +1198,9 @@ def _build_verified_constraint_lines(test_events):
             entry["values"] = event.get("values") or []

     lines: list[str] = []
-    for (model_name, column_name), entry in sorted(grouped.items()):
+    for (model_name, column_name), entry in sorted(
+        grouped.items(), key=lambda kv: (kv[0][0], kv[0][1] or "")
+    ):
         tests = entry["tests"]
         if not column_name:
             continue
